WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.880
A seventy kilogram rider
races down a zip wire.

2
00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:06.830
Now redraw it as a mechanics problem.

3
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:11.240
The rider shrinks to a single
dot, with arrows for the forces.

4
00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.010
So why can a dot stand
in for a whole person?

5
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:18.240
Because seventy kilograms
is tiny next to the Earth?

6
00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:20.500
Because a dot has no mass?

7
00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.060
In this mission, you'll meet the SI units:

8
00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:26.740
the metre, kilogram, second and newton.

9
00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:30.260
You'll find weight as
a force: mass times g,

10
00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:33.810
with g as nine point eight
metres per second squared.

11
00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:36.720
And you'll learn the
modelling words: particle,

12
00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:39.910
light, inextensible, smooth.

13
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:45.090
Your mission: explain why a seventy
kilogram person can be modelled as a dot.
